  "answer": "I can't give you a current peso figure. None of my data sources publish an AUD/ARS rate. The RBA's exchange rate tables cover about 23 currencies, but not the Argentine peso.\n\nWhat I can give you is the Australian dollar against the US dollar, which is the usual bridge for converting to pesos:\n\n- **A$1 = US$0.6947** (RBA, 4pm AEST, 16 October 2026, the latest figure available)\n- That's down from US$0.717 on 1 September 2026, a fall of about 3.1% over that period.\n\nTo get the peso figure, multiply by the current USD/ARS rate. Argentina has had several exchange rates (official, MEP and \"blue\" or parallel), and they can differ a lot, so check which one you need. The Banco Central de la República Argentina publishes the official rate, and financial sites such as Ámbito or Bloomberg show the others.",
